Compile out the pre-1.1.0 OpenSSL locking callbacks for OpenSSL 1.1.0 and later.

CRYPTO_set_locking_callback() was removed in OpenSSL 1.1.0, where locking
became internal to libcrypto. The two calls to it in src/protocol/ssl.cc sit
outside the existing OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER guards, so on any modern OpenSSL
they are hard compile errors:

    src/protocol/ssl.cc:119: error: 'CRYPTO_set_locking_callback' was not declared
    src/protocol/ssl.cc:174: error: 'CRYPTO_set_locking_callback' was not declared

Termux builds php 8.5.1 with --with-openssl=$TERMUX_PREFIX against OpenSSL
3.6.3. That makes php-config report openssl as enabled, and
include/openswoole_compat.h maps SW_USE_OPENSSL to OSW_USE_OPENSSL, so this
file is compiled with the SSL paths active even though the extension's own
--enable-openssl defaults to no. Dropping --with-openssl-dir from the package
therefore does not avoid this.

The lock_array bookkeeping only exists to feed those callbacks, so it is
guarded along with them rather than left in place.

Upstream carries no OpenSSL 3 support in any release (checked master, v26.2.0,
v25.2.0 and v22.1.2: none reference 0x30000000, OPENSSL_VERSION_MAJOR,
OSSL_PARAM or EVP_MD_fetch), so this has to be a local patch.
--- a/src/protocol/ssl.cc	2026-09-26 16:25:05.600073324 +0700
+++ b/src/protocol/ssl.cc	2026-09-26 16:25:13.128073321 +0700
@@ -111,12 +111,15 @@
 
     OPENSSL_free(lock_array);
 
-#if OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER >= OPENSSL_VERSION_1_0_0
+#if OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER >= 0x10100000L
+    /* OpenSSL >= 1.1.0 does its own locking; there is no callback to clear. */
+#elif OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER >= OPENSSL_VERSION_1_0_0
     (void) CRYPTO_THREADID_set_callback(nullptr);
+    CRYPTO_set_locking_callback(nullptr);
 #else
     CRYPTO_set_id_callback(nullptr);
-#endif
     CRYPTO_set_locking_callback(nullptr);
+#endif
     openssl_init = false;
     openssl_thread_safety_init = false;
 }
@@ -165,13 +168,15 @@
         pthread_mutex_init(&(lock_array[i]), nullptr);
     }
 
-#if OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER >= OPENSSL_VERSION_1_0_0
+#if OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER >= 0x10100000L
+    /* OpenSSL >= 1.1.0 does its own locking; no callback to install. */
+#elif OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER >= OPENSSL_VERSION_1_0_0
     (void) CRYPTO_THREADID_set_callback(openswoole_ssl_id_callback);
+    CRYPTO_set_locking_callback(openswoole_ssl_lock_callback);
 #else
     CRYPTO_set_id_callback(openswoole_ssl_id_callback);
-#endif
-
     CRYPTO_set_locking_callback(openswoole_ssl_lock_callback);
+#endif
     openssl_thread_safety_init = true;
 }
 
